// BT-3916 (ADR 0133): a class (the receiver is the class object) with class-side `do:` and its
// own `anySatisfy:` whose semantics differ from the fold over `do:` (it looks only
// at the first element). A writing block sent `anySatisfy:` is refused rather
// than folded over `do:`. Driven by adr0133enumerable_user_test.bt.

Object subclass: Adr0133EnumerableObjectOwnAny

  class do: block =>
    block value: 1
    block value: 2
    block value: 3
    nil

  class anySatisfy: block => block value: 1
